.SH 標準規格
POSIX.1\-2008.
.SH 歴史
glibc 2.1.  POSIX.1\-2001.
.P
これは UNIX 98 疑似端末仕様の一部である。 \fBpts\fP(4) を参照。
.P
Historical systems implemented this function via a set\-user\-ID helper binary
called "pt_chown".  glibc on Linux before glibc 2.33 could do so as well, in
order to support configurations with only BSD pseudoterminals; this support
has been removed.  On modern systems this is either a no\-op \[em]with
permissions configured on pty allocation, as is the case on Linux\[em] or an
\fBioctl\fP(2).
